## Summary
- Clear the zalouser probe timeout handle once the auth lookup resolves or rejects.
- Keep the existing timeout fallback behavior for slow auth lookups.
- Collision check: open PR file search returned no PR modifying extensions/zalouser/src/probe.ts before opening.

## Verification
- node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-zalo.config.ts extensions/zalouser/src/probe.test.ts -t "clears the probe timeout after auth resolves" --reporter verbose - passed, 1 focused spec.
- node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/zalouser/src/probe.test.ts - passed, 1 file / 6 specs.
- Non-mocked runtime comparison below: current main leaves one fallback probe timer pending after the real local session lookup returns; this branch clears it before returning.
- git diff --check - passed.

## Real behavior proof
Behavior or issue addressed: Zalouser probe calls with a timeout now clear the scheduled fallback timer after the auth lookup completes or fails, so a stale timer is not left behind after the real probe lookup path returns before the timeout.

Real environment tested: Local OpenClaw checkout on Linux, Node.js v22.22.0. The comparison uses the real probeZalouser implementation and real getZaloUserInfo(profile) local session lookup path with a disposable profile name that has no saved Zalo session. No external Zalo account, phone number, endpoint, token, or credential is used.

Exact steps or command run after this patch:
~~~bash
node --import tsx --input-type=module <<'EOF_SCRIPT'
import { probeZalouser } from './extensions/zalouser/src/probe.ts';

const realSetTimeout = globalThis.setTimeout;
const realClearTimeout = globalThis.clearTimeout;
const active = new Set();

globalThis.setTimeout = ((fn, ms, ...args) => {
  const handle = realSetTimeout(fn, ms, ...args);
  active.add(handle);
  console.log('[timer] scheduled ' + ms);
  return handle;
});

globalThis.clearTimeout = ((handle) => {
  const had = active.delete(handle);
  console.log('[timer] cleared had=' + had);
  return realClearTimeout(handle);
});

const result = await probeZalouser('proof-no-session', 10);
console.log(JSON.stringify({ result, activeProbeTimersAfterReturn: active.size }));
for (const handle of active) realClearTimeout(handle);
globalThis.setTimeout = realSetTimeout;
globalThis.clearTimeout = realClearTimeout;
EOF_SCRIPT
~~~

Evidence before fix on current main (65805e519d; upstream/main still has the same extensions/zalouser/src/probe.ts timeout race shape):
~~~text
[timer] scheduled 1000
{"result":{"ok":false,"error":"No saved Zalo session for profile \"proof-no-session\""},"activeProbeTimersAfterReturn":1}
~~~

Evidence after fix on this PR branch (db7e5b74df):
~~~text
[timer] scheduled 1000
[timer] cleared had=true
{"result":{"ok":false,"error":"No saved Zalo session for profile \"proof-no-session\""},"activeProbeTimersAfterReturn":0}
~~~

Observed result after fix: The real Zalouser probe lookup path still reports the expected no-session error for a disposable profile, but the fallback timeout handle is cleared before probeZalouser returns. Current main returns with one fallback probe timer still pending.

What was not tested: No external Zalo account login was exercised. This is a local non-mocked runtime transcript for the real local session lookup path, not a full live authenticated Zalouser account proof.

